+crew#726: the founder's fast-gates blueprint (2026-08-31, verbatim record in the claude-estate founder docs at 2026-08-31T0225Z), rule 1: a laptop never runs a test suite in a git hook — local hooks are lint and static analysis; CI on the pull request runs the suite. Measured cause: four sessions each ran the pre-push suite (13-52 minutes) at once on 2026-08-30/31; load hit 530 and pushes were refused on subprocess.TimeoutExpired reds with zero real failures (session a7b41022 push log: 26 reds = 3 real + 23 timeouts). The gate was grading the machine's load, not the branch.
+
+Optimised: 3 steps -> 1, 2 round trips -> 1; cut: the machine-wide push lock and the cheap-file floor pruning, both subsumed by one 9-line early exit that stops local suite runs entirely (nothing long runs locally, so nothing needs a lock).
+
+Verify: `python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_incident_crew726_local_hooks_never_run_suites.py`
+
+## Options considered
+- Keep local suites but add a machine-wide flock so they queue: still burns 13-52 minutes per push serially, still babysits (blueprint rule 4), and a queue four deep is an hour of latency. Rejected.
+- Delete bin/idp-tests-for from the hook entirely: loses the printed selection (the record of what CI will grade) and the CI path that reuses this selector. Rejected.
+- Chosen: an early exit in the selector itself — local prints the selection and exits 0; CI (CI env set) behavior is byte-identical; TESTS_FOR_RUN=1 keeps the old local run for hand debugging.
+
+## Architecture laws
+- LAW 1 zero-gravity: `bin/idp-tests-for` -> the pre-push hook rung every idp push runs
+- LAW 2 fractal: `bash -n bin/idp-tests-for && bin/idp-tests-for --list`
+- LAW 3 nervous system: tests/test_incident_crew726_local_hooks_never_run_suites.py (3: the laptop road skips and still prints the selection; CI reaches the runner unchanged; TESTS_FOR_RUN=1 keeps the hand-debug road)
+- LAW 4 calibration: 60-second command budget (founder rule 3); the remaining local rungs run in seconds
+Cost-delta-usd-month: 0 (CI runs what it already ran; laptops stop burning 13-52 min per push)
+Tile: none — developer tooling; the PR checks page is the surface
+
+## Definition of done
+1. Tracked item — crew#726 D1 (founder ruling on the record, comment 5473019074)
+2. Code or config — bin/idp-tests-for early exit outside CI + tests/test_incident_crew726_local_hooks_never_run_suites.py
+3. Gate proved both ways — before: push refused after 52 min on timeout reds (task by8hi53kh); after: this branch's own push ran the hook in seconds and the suite runs here in CI
+4. Reference doc — crew#726 decision record + the founder document named above
+5. How-to and demo — push any idp branch: the hook prints "tests-for: local run skipped (R58 fast-gates)" and CI grades the PR
+6. Catalog entity — existing idp component
+7. Operational proof — this PR's own CI run is the selector running in CI mode
+8. Scheduled re-grade — every push exercises the local path; every PR exercises the CI path
+9. Standard row — CI; no provider names, no hardcoded paths added
+10. Evidence block — this PR's green checks page
+Standard: CI
+
